    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35447" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-sanctus</span></b> , a, um, adj.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very
			sacred</i> or <i>holy</i>: CONIVX, Inscr. Afr. ap.
			Rénier, 4414.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-sanctē</span></b> , <i>very sacredly</i> or <i>religiously</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dejerare,</span>”
				<i>to swear solemnly</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Hec. 5, 2, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jurare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 10</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Ner. 35</span></i>.</div>
